{"input_text": "Question: Let $0 \leq p \leq 1$, $n \in \mathbb{N}_0$ and consider $$\sum_{i = 0}^{\lfloor n/2 \rfloor} {n \choose 2i}p^{2i}(1 - p)^{n - 2i}$$ Has anyone a hint for me how I can calculate the sum?  

Answer: $$
\begin{align}
\sum_k\binom{n}{2k}p^{2k}(1-p)^{n-2k}
&=\frac12\left[\sum_k\binom{n}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-k}+\sum_k(-1)^k\binom{n}{k}p^k(1-p)^{n-k}\right]\\[6pt]
&=\frac12\left[1+(1-2p)^n\right]
\end{align}
$$ 
